# Changelog
## [0.3.1] - 2026-11-04
### Breaking changes
 - N/A

### New features
 - N/A

### Bug fixes
 - Use netlink-proto 0.14.1. (ce4ee35)
 - doc: READMD.md: add example code on removing multiple peers. (5b17892)

## [0.3.0] - 2026-09-14
### Breaking changes
 - API break: mark `ErrorKind` as `#[non_exhaustive]`. (4680ff0)

### New features
 - Add API to remove a wireguard peer. (6bb8874)

### Bug fixes
 - fix: enforce `IFNAMSIZ` for interface names. (749881e)
 - fix: never attach a raw kernel echo to errors. (df1db24)
 - fix: validate peer keys and allowed IP prefixes. (421030d)
 - fix: handle netlink acknowledgements and dump results. (14c2c99)
 - fix: reject out of range last handshake time. (0abc6f2)
 - fix: never report key material in errors. (34a87a9)
 - fix: coalesce peers split over several dump replies. (0fe1a35)
 - fix: split large configuration over several messages. (496ee96)
 - fix: apply `get_by_name()` result back with `set()`. (5edc23d)

## [0.2.0] - 2026-08-18
### Breaking changes
 - Use latest rust-netlink crates. (e85cafc)
 - Do not reexport netlink-packet-wireguard. (6484172)

### New features
 - Add support flags of device, peer and allowed-ip. (691f911)

### Bug fixes
 - fix: fetch all wireguard peers. (1a41702)

